          realWorldAnalogy: "Class methods are like factory settings - they affect how objects are made.",
          content: `Class Method Syntax

class MyClass:
    @classmethod
    def class_method(cls):
        return cls

Factory Method

class Person:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age
    
    @classmethod
    def from_birth_year(cls, name, birth_year):
        age = 2024 - birth_year
        return cls(name, age)`,
          codeExamples: [
            {
              id: "ch24-classmethods",
