          realWorldAnalogy: "Magic methods are like hidden controls - they define how objects interact with Python.",
          content: `String Representation

class Point:
    def __init__(self, x, y):
        self.x = x
        self.y = y
    
    def __str__(self):
        return f\"Point({self.x}, {self.y})\"
    
    def __repr__(self):
        return f\"Point({self.x}, {self.y})\"

Operator Overloading

class Vector:
    def __add__(self, other):
        return Vector(self.x + other.x, self.y + other.y)`,
          codeExamples: [
            {
              id: "ch26-magic",
