          realWorldAnalogy: "Metaclasses are like class factories - they define how classes are made.",
          content: `Creating Metaclasses

class Meta(type):\n    def __new__(cls, name, bases, namespace):\n        # Modify class creation\n        return super().__new__(cls, name, bases, namespace)\n\nUsing Metaclasses

class MyClass(metaclass=Meta):\n    pass

Common Uses\n- Singleton pattern\n- Register classes\n- Add methods automatically`,
          codeExamples: [
            {
              id: "ch35-metaclasses",
              title: "Metaclasses",
              description: "Custom class creation",
              code: { python: "class Singleton(type):\n    _instances = {}\n    def __call__(cls, *args, **kwargs):\n        if cls not in cls._instances:\n            cls._instances[cls] = super().__call__(*args, **kwargs)\n        return cls._instances[cls]\n\nclass Database(metaclass=Singleton):\n    pass\n\nprint(Database() is Database())  # True" },
              explanation: "Metaclasses control class creation and behavior."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
