          whyItMatters: "Iterators enable custom iteration behavior for your objects.",
          realWorldAnalogy: "Iterators are like playlists - you go through items one by one.",
          content: `Iterator Protocol

class Counter:
    def __iter__(self):
        self.n = 0
        return self
    
    def __next__(self):
        self.n += 1
        if self.n > 5:
            raise StopIteration
        return self.n

Using iter() and next()

iterator = iter([1, 2, 3])
print(next(iterator))  # 1`,
          codeExamples: [
            {
              id: "ch41-iterators",
              title: "Custom Iterator",
              description: "Creating iterators",
              code: { python: "class Countdown:\n    def __init__(self, start):\n        self.current = start\n    \n    def __iter__(self):\n        return self\n    \n    def __next__(self):\n        if self.current <= 0:\n            raise StopIteration\n        self.current -= 1\n        return self.current + 1\n\nfor num in Countdown(3):\n    print(num)  # 3, 2, 1" },
              explanation: "Implement __iter__ and __next__ for custom iteration."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      exercises: [
        {
          id: "ch41-ex1",
          title: "Range Iterator",
          difficulty: 1,
          description: "Create a custom range iterator.",
          requirements: ["Implement __iter__ and __next__", "Iterate from start to end"],
          starterCode: { python: "class MyRange:\n    def __init__(self, start, end):\n        self.start = start\n        self.end = end\n    \n    # Implement iterator protocol" },
          hints: ["__iter__ returns self", "__next__ returns next value"],
          solution: { python: "class MyRange:\n    def __init__(self, start, end):\n        self.start = start\n        self.end = end\n        self.current = start\n    \n    def __iter__(self):\n        self.current = self.start\n        return self\n    \n    def __next__(self):\n        if self.current >= self.end:\n            raise StopIteration\n        result = self.current\n        self.current += 1\n        return result" },
          solutionExplanation: "Iterators implement the iteration protocol."
        }
      ],
